 > You mentioned this earlier too, but it is
 > backwards.  The chance of leaving bones increases
 > with depth.

Okay, the problem (for me) is that the language in
the source comment in src/bones.c is ambiguous:

179     if(depth(&u.uz) <= 0 ||		/* bulletproofing for endgame */
180        (!rn2(1 + (depth(&u.uz)>>2))	/* fewer ghosts on low levels */

... if not on astral OR
... rn2(1 + int(dungeon_depth/4)) is zero
... return "don't drop bones file".

Which looks like a bug; I think that formulation
using a logical OR and a positive dungeon level
just resolves to "not on astral" -- since OR is a
shortcut operator, the right hand side never gets
evaluated if not on astral.

Probably to do what it intended the code should
instead read

179     if (!((depth(&u.uz) >= 0) &&       /* bulletproofing for endgame */
180        (rn2(1 + (depth(&u.uz)>>2))))) /* fewer ghosts on low levels */

... if NOT (not on astral AND
... rn2(1 + int(dungeon_depth/4) isn't zero))
... return "don't drop bones file"

         [Never, in writing code for maintainability,
         trust the _next_ maintainer to remember the
         order of operator precedence and so read
         your code the way you intended it; instead,
         fully parenthesize the code so that there is
         no ambiguity on either end.]

I read "low" as "lower in the dungeon", but
apparently (per the code) it is meant as "lower in
level ID number". Much better would be that the
comment read "/* more ghosts on deeper levels */"
to use less ambiguous terminology.

         [Anybody who can confirm that the current
         code is a bug and knows how to submit a bug
         report to the DevTeam, please do so; painful
         experiences on the Mozilla bugzilla bug
         reporting board have put me permanently out
         of the bug reporting business.]

